{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06QB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{X} \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\mathcal{X} \\times \\mathcal{X} \\ar[d] \\\\\n&\n\\mathcal{Y} \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{Y} \\times \\mathcal{Y}\n}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{proposition-when-gerbe-over}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-surjection-from-quasi-compact}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-descent-quasi-compact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:996edf6372aa45b2a24b2bdcbfff5febbe6dc695cbb8b0100cc1e6168e296fc3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3a3c1bf703d48ab7b4b27755be0c5979b4aa48c078b8b15b048b18bc37475823", "source_text": "Consider the diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nBy Proposition <REF_0001> we find that\nthe arrow on the top left is surjective. Since the composition\nof the top horizontal arrows is quasi-compact, we conclude\nthat the top right arrow is quasi-compact by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nThe square is cartesian and the right vertical arrow is\nsurjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation.\nThus we conclude by Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:81b0084a4bcaf8fc75fea2cd95d48a3f7cc9527991506e3408c3b7ea9de3d1b1", "unit_id": "tag:0DQL:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06QB", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:756a0a47afcf908787bd94e177bde545fa4de7592191f1adc5af1b70e650ae7c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma tells us that residual gerbes exist for all points\non any algebraic stack which is a gerbe.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c003bf1a54b3655ebceedcb8c42692c8951c2e90d96dd787d7d3a9f405e7cfa7", "unit_id": "tag:06QB:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06QB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$x$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-gerbe-residual-gerbe-exists}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8ff2587b4e73f9194a39ac0dca4d87d289d687e361b14b6ee9ec7039c7b47bb8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b2e4e3106808c63e40ccf3edb50b7c5b7563f892c8259b243380f2c5a41ad45c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack. If <MATH_0002> is a gerbe\nthen for every <MATH_0003> the residual gerbe of <MATH_0004>\nat <MATH_0005> exists.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f8c7ad09b1fb10c907b860a07c9b63a3be291f94ad96756711fb63fc13490369", "unit_id": "tag:06RA:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06QB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\pi : \\mathcal{X} \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$Z_x \\to X$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$x$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{Z} = \\mathcal{X} \\times_X Z_x$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0011": "$Z_x$", "MATH_0012": "$|\\mathcal{Z}| = |Z_x|$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to Z_x$", "MATH_0014": "$\\pi$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{Z}_x$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0018": "$x$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{Z}_x = \\mathcal{Z}_{red}$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0021": "$|\\mathcal{Z}_{red}|$", "MATH_0022": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{decent-spaces-definition-residual-space}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-gerbe}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-gerbe-bijection-points}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-gerbe-fppf}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-finite-presentation}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-locally-finite-type-locally-noetherian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:be727867a5d6ad243de0a1d6b584dbcd0b0c2fbfdf200560bbfd3e484b55849a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dcc9cee74b1c643b41bb9a841886c685a46f938416aeca49f3522c404e61e399", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism from <MATH_0002> into\nan algebraic space <MATH_0003> which turns <MATH_0004> into a gerbe over <MATH_0005>.\nLet <MATH_0006> be the residual space of <MATH_0007> at <MATH_0008>, see\nDecent Spaces, Definition <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0009>. By\nLemma <REF_0002>\nthe algebraic stack <MATH_0010> is a gerbe over <MATH_0011>.\nHence <MATH_0012>\n(Lemma <REF_0003>)\nis a singleton. Since <MATH_0013> is locally of finite presentation\nas a base change of <MATH_0014> (see\nLemmas <REF_0004> and <REF_0005>)\nwe see that <MATH_0015> is locally Noetherian, see\nLemma <REF_0006>.\nThus the residual gerbe <MATH_0016> of <MATH_0017> at <MATH_0018>\nexists and is equal to <MATH_0019> the reduction\nof the algebraic stack <MATH_0020>. Namely, we have seen above\nthat <MATH_0021> is a singleton mapping to <MATH_0022>,\nit is reduced by construction, and it is locally Noetherian (as the\nreduction of a locally Noetherian algebraic stack is locally Noetherian,\ndetails omitted).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:67ccdc92c34df5e4c87177cd19b0a44dbd27aa8425c2ef9d5f9010c609c2a758", "unit_id": "tag:06RA:proof"}
